<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina says 1996/97 wool exports up 18.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Argentina says 1996/97 wool exports up 18.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina exported 38,494 clean tonnes of wool in its 1996/97 season, up by 18.3 percent from 1995/96, the government's Agricultural Secretariat said Tuesday.</p>
<p>But lower prices meant that FOB export receipts slipped to $132.5 million from $150.6 million the previous season. Argentina's wool season runs from July to March.</p>
<p>The secretariat provided the following list of export destinations (figures in tonnes, previous season in brackets):</p>
<p>   Italy:	     8,311  (5,519)</p>
<p>   Germany:	   7,734  (5,448)</p>
<p>   China:	     6,056  (5,599)</p>
<p>   France:	    3,026  (2,733)</p>
<p>   Belgium:	   2,547    (845)</p>
<p>   India		1,817  (2,093)</p>
<p>   Hong Kong	  1,799  (1,673)</p>
<p>   Uruguay	    1,108  (1,971)</p>
<p>   Mexico		 991    (719)</p>
<p>   Japan		  660    (881)</p>
<p>   Chile		  593    (487)</p>
<p>   Peru		   573    (355)</p>
<p>   Spain		  490    (448)</p>
<p>   Taiwan		 489    (807)</p>
<p>   Britain		483    (811)</p>
<p>   Others	     1,817  (2,160)</p>
<p>   Total	     38,494 (32,549)</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
</text>
